#: ../../../reference/interfaces/custom-device-interface.md:2
msgid "custom-device interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/custom-device-interface.md:4
msgid ""
"The `custom-device` interface permits access to a device of a specific class "
"and model without requiring the creation of an interface for that device "
"alone. It’s intended to be used with {ref}`Ubuntu Core <ref-glossary_ubuntu-"
"core>` and its scope and specification are defined as part of the {ref}"
"`gadget snap <reference-development-yaml-schemas-the-gadget-snap>` for the "
"deployed Ubuntu Core image."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/custom-device-interface.md:6
msgid ""
"To permit access, the application snaps define a custom-device plug and the "
"[gadget snap](https://documentation.ubuntu.com/core/reference/gadget-snap-"
"format/) defines a custom-device slot, where both the plug and the slot have "
"the identically-named `custom-device` attribute."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/custom-device-interface.md:8
msgid ""
"Under specific and appropriate circumstances, it is possible to define the "
"slot directly from the consuming application itself, together with the plug, "
"which is an acceptable approach for applications that will be widely "
"distributed but support very specific hardware."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/custom-device-interface.md:10
msgid ""
"Using the custom-device requires {ref}`Store approval and permissions "
"<interfaces-process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks>`, both to allow "
"the presence of the slot, and to set up elements such as the slot self-"
"connecting exactly to the plug on the app. The more specific the tagging "
"information provided by the slot, the easier it will be to allow for this."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/custom-device-interface.md:12
msgid ""
"The slot-side of the interface is used to derive which _udev_ rules are "
"provided to the plug-side of the connection:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/custom-device-interface.md:14
msgid ""
"slots:\n"
"  dual-sd:\n"
"    interface: custom-device\n"
"    custom-device: my-dual-sd-device\n"
"    devices:\n"
"      - /dev/DualSD\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/custom-device-interface.md:23
msgid ""
"To prevent connection to arbitrary custom-device slots, the plug and slot "
"must share the same custom-device attributes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/custom-device-interface.md:25
msgid ""
"plugs:\n"
"  dual-sd:\n"
"    interface: custom-device\n"
"    custom-device: my-dual-sd-device\n"
"apps:\n"
"  app:\n"
"    plugs: [dual-sd]\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/custom-device-interface.md:35
msgid ""
"When the slot and plug are connected, a udev rule is automatically generated "
"and tagged for the plug side for each device path in the `devices` and `read-"
"devices` attributes, such as:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/custom-device-interface.md:37
msgid "KERNEL==\"DualSD\",\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/custom-device-interface.md:41
msgid ""
"Note that here, the default udev `KERNEL` rule is the full device path "
"following the leading `/dev/`. Depending on the device drivers, some devices "
"expect the `KERNEL` rule to be only the basename of the device path, even if "
"that device is in a subdirectory of `/dev/`. For this reason, when `udev-"
"tagging` attributes are not given for a device which is in a subdirectory of "
"`/dev/`, default `KERNEL` rules are generated for both the basename and for "
"the full device path following the leading `/dev/`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/custom-device-interface.md:43
msgid ""
"If the `udev-tagging` attribute is used, this default udev rule is replaced "
"with more specific rules, as described below. When a device name in the "
"`kernel` attribute does not match the device path listed in the `devices` "
"section, such as if the `KERNEL` udev attribute is different than the `/"
"dev/...` path, an optional `for-device` attribute can be added to establish "
"a correspondence, such that both udev matching rules and the AppArmor "
"profile is generated correctly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/custom-device-interface.md:45
msgid ""
"Requires snapd version *2.55+*, while `udev-tagging.for-device` attribute "
"support requires snapd version *2.66+*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/custom-device-interface.md:50
msgid "Developer details"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/custom-device-interface.md:52
msgid ""
"**{ref}`Auto-connect <explanation-interfaces-interface-auto-connection>`**: "
"no</br> **{ref}`Super-privileged <reference-operations-interfaces-super-"
"privileged-interfaces>`**: yes</br>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/custom-device-interface.md:52
#: ../../../reference/interfaces/custom-device-interface.md:56
#: ../../../reference/interfaces/custom-device-interface.md:58
#: ../../../reference/interfaces/custom-device-interface.md:61
#: ../../../reference/interfaces/custom-device-interface.md:63
msgid "</br>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/custom-device-interface.md:55
msgid "**Attributes**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/custom-device-interface.md:56
msgid ""
"`custom-device` (optional) (plug, slot): A label for the custom device.</br> "
"The label must be identical across the plug and slot connections.</br>If "
"omitted, the label defaults to either local slot name or local plug name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/custom-device-interface.md:58
msgid ""
"`devices` (slot): paths to device nodes.</br>   Example: `devices: [/dev/"
"input/event[0-9], /dev/input/mice]`</br>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/custom-device-interface.md:60
msgid "`files` (optional) (slot):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/custom-device-interface.md:61
msgid ""
"`read` (slot): list of files and/or directories for read-only access by the "
"device.</br>   Example:  `read: [ /dev/input/by-id/* ]`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/custom-device-interface.md:63
msgid ""
"`write` (slot): list of files and/or directories for read/write access by "
"the device.</br>   Example: `write: [ /etc/file-write, /etc/dir-write ]`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/custom-device-interface.md:65
msgid ""
"`read-devices` (optional) (slot): paths to device nodes for read-only "
"access.   Example: `read-devices: [ /dev/js* ]`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/custom-device-interface.md:67
msgid ""
"`udev-tagging` (optional): used to tailor the generated udev rules. Can be "
"one of the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/custom-device-interface.md:68
msgid ""
"`kernel`: (mandatory): maps to the string used as the udev `KERNEL==` filter "
"rule."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/custom-device-interface.md:69
msgid "`subsystem`: corresponds to the `SUBSYSTEM==` filters in a udev rule."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/custom-device-interface.md:70
msgid ""
"`environment`: a map of expected environment variables for the udev rule to "
"match with `ENV{...}==\"...\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/custom-device-interface.md:71
msgid "`attributes`: a map of attributes used with `ATTR{...}==\"...\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/custom-device-interface.md:72
msgid ""
"`for-device`: indicates which device the `udev-tagging` snippet refers to"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/custom-device-interface.md:74
msgid "Code examples"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/custom-device-interface.md:76
msgid ""
"A truncated example showing how the subsystem and attributes can be used:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/custom-device-interface.md:78
msgid ""
"   udev-tagging:\n"
"     - kernel: hiddev0\n"
"       subsystem: usb\n"
"       attributes:\n"
"         idVendor: \"0x03f0\" # HP\n"
"     - kernel: hiddev1\n"
"       subsystem: usb\n"
"       attributes:\n"
"         idVendor: \"0x03fc\" # ECS\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/custom-device-interface.md:90
msgid ""
"An example slot declaration showing the how the kernel environment settings "
"can be used with a custom joystick interface:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/custom-device-interface.md:92
msgid ""
"slots:\n"
"  hwdev:\n"
"    interface: custom-device\n"
"    custom-device: custom-joystick\n"
"    devices:\n"
"      - /dev/input/js{[0-9],[12][0-9],3[01]}\n"
"      - /dev/input/event[0-9]*\n"
"    files:\n"
"      read:\n"
"        - /run/udev/data/c13:{6[5-9],[7-9][0-9],[1-9][0-9][0-9]*}\n"
"        - /run/udev/data/c13:{[0-9],[12][0-9],3[01]}\n"
"        - /sys/devices/**/input[0-9]*/capabilities/*\n"
"    udev-tagging:\n"
"      - kernel: input/event[0-9]*\n"
"        subsystem: input\n"
"        environment:\n"
"          ID_INPUT_JOYSTICK: \"1\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/custom-device-interface.md:112
msgid "The above example will generate the following udev tags:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/custom-device-interface.md:114
msgid ""
"spec.TagDevice(`KERNEL==\"js{[0-9],[12][0-9],3[01]}\"`)\n"
"spec.TagDevice(`KERNEL==\"input/js{[0-9],[12][0-9],3[01]}\"`)\n"
"spec.TagDevice(`SUBSYSTEM==\"input\", KERNEL==\"input/event[0-9]*\", "
"ENV{ID_INPUT_JOYSTICK}==\"1\"`)\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/custom-device-interface.md:120
msgid "The following example shows the `udev-tagging` syntax:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/custom-device-interface.md:122
msgid ""
"   slots:\n"
"      v4l:\n"
"        interface: custom-device\n"
"        devices:\n"
"          - /dev/video[0-9]\n"
"        files:\n"
"          read:\n"
"            - /sys/bus/usb/devices\n"
"            - /sys/class/video4linux\n"
"            - /sys/kernel/debug/sleep_time\n"
"          write:\n"
"            - /proc/sys/vm/stat_interval\n"
"        udev-tagging:\n"
"          - kernel: video[0-9]\n"
"            subsystem: v4l\n"
"            environment:\n"
"              var1: foo\n"
"              var2: bar\n"
"            attributes:\n"
"              attr1: one\n"
"              attr2: two\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/custom-device-interface.md:146
msgid ""
"An additional example, showing how to match udev rules with a device which "
"appears at a different path under `/dev/..`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/custom-device-interface.md:148
msgid ""
"   slots:\n"
"      msr:\n"
"        interface: custom-device\n"
"        devices:\n"
"          - /dev/cpu/[0-9]*/msr\n"
"        udev-tagging:\n"
"          - kernel: msr[0-9]*\n"
"            subsystem: msr\n"
"            for-device: /dev/cpu/[0-9]*/msr\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/custom-device-interface.md:160
msgid ""
"The above example generates a udev rule to match `KERNEL==\"msr[0-9]*\", "
"SUBSYSTEM==\"msr\"` and an AppArmor rule allowing read/write access through "
"`/dev/cpu/[0-9]*/msr`."
msgstr ""

